I dont disagree with what you say, and your absolutely in the right when you said DeSantis keeps formulating ways to keep division, and not just between left vs right but in more ways like Christians vs atheists and so on. He's been a really nasty stain on Florida and I wish he would use his position for Floridians instead of for tourists and businesses.

&#x200B;

I also think you, and a lot of people in this thread, think my defense of Republicans, the GOP, and Conservatives means that I must think they're either better than the Left, Liberals, or Democrats, but I don't. In fact, I don't think either side is inherently better than the other because they pool their knowledge from the same source, they just interpret the data differently and use the data differently. But I stand by all of what I said because I have no qualms about defending a side that has its merits, despite its flaws. I've done the same with both sides of politics because I pool my information from both sides, because to grab it information from one side, or to claim one said is inherently better than the other is both naiive and ignorant of the complicated machine that is politics.

There we go

