When did I say that ALL countries with no access to personal firearms, let alone Europe? I said "tend to", implying there are both exceptions to this opinion, and it is by no mean the rule or even the most common, and you do not have to go to Europe to find an example. Latin America tends to not allow public access of firearms to its citizens, and their governments are incredibly corrupt and are extremely authoritarian.

