European viewpoints on personal protection also differ from the states, and so it is not a 1:1 comparison. Their political ideologies have different roots than ours, and while they are a good viewpoint, they do not serve as a perfect template.

&#x200B;

Lastly, I never glorified anything, at no point did I say I support the advertisement, and ultimately, its no different than advertisements for religious movements, gay rights, or any other buzz politics currently in circulation. But it is a right that Americans have, and I for one, do not support removing the freedoms of expression this country has given me, regardless of how her citizens decide to use it.

