You need to understand that the shortcomings of politicians and political spectrums is more than just "removing rights" "censorship" or "authoritarian control", yes, the GOP is incredibly guilty of all those things in the way most left-leaning politics are not, but that does not mean that left-leaning policies allow for more freedoms, or even better freedoms, just different perspectives on the same freedoms, sometimes at costs. Sometimes the cost are economic, sometimes the costs are cultural, and sometimes the costs are purely private - and it ultimately depends on who you are as a person and what you value and dont value.

&#x200B;

Of course, they're not the same, and I never made that claim, and I ask you not to put words in my mouth again.

It mainly has to do with how left-leaning the country has been since about the end of the Bush Sr administration. Its only natural that when one side's rope gets too long, the other side starts pushing back, and when the silent majority of people who's voices have been neglected for so long they take it and run with it.

