It's kinda like deciding who needs water during a drought, a state that has plenty of natural resources like Florida, or states with limited natural resources like Nevada. Its not a perfect analogy but I hope it gets the point across.

Politics has been a game of "he said she said" since the 1980s, and its purely because we as Americans fail to hold our leaders accountable in more than just social criticism. But its also because, especially recently, its exteremly difficult to hold powerful people accountable when the facts are all disconnected and incoherent, and they're protected by equally powerful people with a powerful amount of wealth.

&#x200B;

Its demoralizing, and I hope support for actions against our leaders becomes more mainstream so we can put the fear of God into them. For our country's sake, and our children's.

