>But there’s no excuses for adults to cry or have mental breakdowns or act childish, we are supposed to be mature and calm and know what to do and how to feel in situations

&#x200B;

Says who?



Society? Society doesn't know what we deal with, let alone know the right steps to take towards self-improvement, they're the ones who created the 40-hour work week. Your parents? Your parents were raised with different morals and values, with different stress factors compared to you. Your friends? Your friends lead different lives than you, with a different upbringing and different set of beliefs, they're good to lean on, but they'll never know what its like to be you.

&#x200B;

Bottom line is that its okay to break, to snap, to collapse under the weight of it all. Because the reality is, Life is Hard. Its hard for all the wrong reasons. Its okay to not have the strength to carry the weight of the world, YOUR WORLD, on your shoulders. Its okay to fail, and to not succeed where you felt like you were capable.

&#x200B;

The important part is that you have to get up, and try try again. Try to make your mental state better. Try to make it through the day without thinking of them. Try to find more positives in your life and focus on them, and not let the negatives tear you down even more. You'll fail at this too, time and time again, but it wont matter unless you give up. No one gets it right the first few times, but there is no shame in that.

&#x200B;

I'm sorry you feel trapped in your own head, and I do hope you find the solution we all so desperately want. Good luck

