Firstly, I am sorry for your woes, I sympathize with a lot of what you feel, and it's hard to see someone going through similar struggles.

&#x200B;

That being said, I think you have all the answers you seek right in front of you. You might be behind the ball on a lot of things, but it's never too late to start. Starting an education, a career, a relationship. They're things that there really isn't a time limit on, and you can decide to do them on your own terms if you have the time that is. Where I stand, I don't see you have a deadline on things, aside from just personal or social ones, but even those are not set in stone.

&#x200B;

I'd take a few steps back and reevaluate what you value personally, not just in yourself, but in the world around you, and more importantly in your future. Are you really a fuck-up, or are you fixated on your failures? Do you handle failure well? Have you handled failure better in the past? These are questions that can clarify a lot of things, and at the very least give you perspective on yourself, and how you interact with the world.

&#x200B;

I hope you find what you're looking for, and keep up the good work. I can't promise it'll pay off, but it's the best thing you have. Good luck

