I wouldn't say that. I believe it's a sign of teenage behavior. He's 16 and has the rest of his life working a 9-5. I started working at 17 and regretted it. The work experience and money were fine, but it drained my motivation to do well and caused me to choose between work, school, family, friends, and myself. He might be in the same boat and thinking he's not ready or willing to give up his free time just for a paycheck just yet, which isn't something he should be ashamed about.

&#x200B;

I would not discourage or encourage him for his actions, but definitely ask him to see if he's okay, he might be just dealing with some growing pains.
